   by the system, software, or asset owner.

2. PROHIBITION OF MALICIOUS INTENT:
   Under no circumstances shall the Software or any derivative work be used for:
   a) Unauthorized cyber intrusions, attacks, or unlawful access to computing assets.
   b) Deployment or weaponization of malware, ransomware, or disruptive payloads.
   c) Any activity that violates domestic or international cybersecurity laws, regulations,
      or privacy rights.

3. RESPONSIBLE DISCLOSURE COVENANT:
   Any zero-day vulnerability, credential exposure, or architectural weakness identified
